        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Apple macOS 15 (Sequoia) Security Technical Implementation Guide :: v1r6</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-268451</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-OS-000064-GPOS-00033</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-268451r1131208_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>APPL-15-000190</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The macOS system must configure sudo to log events.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Sudo must be configured to log privilege escalation.

Without logging privilege escalation, it is difficult to identify attempted attacks because no audit trail is available for forensic investigation.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Verify the macOS system is configured to log privilege escalation with the following command:

/usr/bin/sudo /usr/bin/sudo -V | /usr/bin/grep -c "Log when a command is allowed by sudoers"

If the result is not "1", this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content_Ref</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>C-72481r1034291_chk</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the macOS system to log privilege escalation with the following command:

/usr/bin/find /etc/sudoers* -type f -exec sed -i '' '/^Defaults[[:blank:]]*\!log_allowed/s/^/# /' '{}' \;
/bin/echo "Defaults log_allowed" &gt;&gt; /etc/sudoers.d/mscp</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
          <VULN_ATTRIBUTE>False_Negatives</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
          <ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
        </STIG_DATA>
        <STIG_DATA>
